  "summary_en": "December 2020 update of Germany's national AI Strategy, expanding funding to 5 billion euros by 2025. It sets priorities on talent, research, transfer, regulatory framework and society, stressing sustainability, pandemic response and \"AI Made in Europe\". Embodied AI appears only briefly (autonomous driving, aerospace robotics, regulatory sandboxes, product safety).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Raises federal AI funding from 3 to 5 billion euros by 2025",
   "Funds 100 AI professorships and expands the network of AI research centres to at least twelve",
   "Backs regulatory sandboxes and European test fields for autonomous driving",
   "Develops quality infrastructure, standardisation roadmap and certification for safe, trustworthy AI",
   "Supports EU review of product safety and liability law for AI and a central certification body for security-authority AI"
